From 3bc5ca115024a3384028f2532cd131077c4882b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:42:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 35/49] Eden (Doris): fewer wake-up system calls, fewer cut
 render passes; more report data

Speed:
- The GPU thread handed recorded work to the Vulkan worker every 4 draws and
  woke it with a condition-variable notify each time; on Android every notify
  is a futex system call, and the worker made another one for every chunk it
  took. In build 11 that was about 12% of the GPU thread and 9% of the worker.
  Now work goes over every 16 draws, and either side only notifies when the
  other one is actually waiting.
- Every 512 draws Eden submitted, which ends the open render pass; on a tiled
  GPU the rest of that pass then has to store and reload all its attachments.
  Doris now waits for a moment when no render pass is open (up to 2048 draws).

Report (per frame / per 10 s): worker wake-ups, render passes cut by a submit,
memory-protection changes, wait-for-idles, tiled-cache barriers, texture
uploads (and uploads over GPU-drawn contents), garbage-collector removals
(copied back / lost), GPU memory against the collector thresholds.

Profiler: records call stacks (frame-pointer chain, bounded by the thread
stack) and names system-library functions (nearest exported symbol).
